{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "archon-node-kinds",
  "title": "Archon node kinds",
  "description": "Archon's DAG node schema drawn as a hierarchy, top to bottom.\n\n- **Top strip:** color key, the constitution line (\"YAML coordinates. Code computes. Agents judge.\"), and the note that every DAG node extends dagNodeBaseSchema and picks one NODE_MODE_SHAPES key.\n- **Row 1:** **Common fields** (the eight shared fields) beside the **when / trigger_rule grammar**: `when` wires to the atom (Refs, Ops), `trigger_rule` to its four values.\n- **Hub:** the **DAG node** points up to the common fields (\"extends\") and right to the decision **exactly 1 of 11 mode keys**. One trunk runs down the band between columns, branching to each group's modes subsection.\n- **Row 2:** **Agent nodes** (command, prompt, Agent knobs, Claude knobs) | **Pause nodes** (wait → its four forms, approval → its fields, cancel).\n- **Row 3:** **Control nodes** (loop → loop knobs, loop_group, include and workflow → fan_out) | **Code nodes** (bash, script → stdout → output_format check → node output, or red failure with no retry).\n\nColor key: blue = mode key, teal = field/knob/value, orange = choice, violet = DAG node, red = failure.",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "zoom": 1
  },
